### Test Company with Branches Endpoint

@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000

### 1. Get Company with Branches (Efficient for Login)
GET {{baseUrl}}/sys_company/COMP1/with-branches

### Expected Response:
# {
#   "id": "COMP1",
#   "name": "PT. Test Company",
#   "companyLogo": "...",
#   "branches": [
#     {
#       "id": "BR001",
#       "name": "Cabang Jakarta",
#       "iStatus": "Active"
#     },
#     {
#       "id": "BR002",
#       "name": "Cabang Bandung",
#       "iStatus": "Active"
#     }
#   ],
#   ... (other company fields)
# }

### 2. Compare with Separate Calls (Old Way)
# First get company
GET {{baseUrl}}/sys_company/COMP1

###
# Then get branches
GET {{baseUrl}}/sys_branch/company/COMP1

### Benefits of /with-branches endpoint:
# ✅ Single HTTP request instead of 2
# ✅ Atomic operation - guaranteed consistency
# ✅ Lower latency
# ✅ Only returns active branches
# ✅ Branches already sorted by name

